[agent] The FTI pipeline is built end-to-end on the platform. Here is the outcome.
[agent] ## Completed on the platform (Vertex AI + BigQuery feature store)
[agent] | Step | Deliverable | Where | Result |
[agent] |---|---|---|---|
[agent] | **F** — feature engineering | `airqf3f1d8` | BQ table in `$GCP_BQ_DATASET` | 979 rows; weather + `pm25_lag1`, seasonal (`month`, `doy_sin/cos`), `temp_hum`, `pm25_roll7`, `feature_timestamp` key `date` |
[agent] | **T** — training dataset | `airqtdf3f1d8` | BQ table | modeling features (forecast-available only) + `pm25` label |
[agent] | **T** — model + metrics | `airqmodelf3f1d8` → Vertex model `mlpab0ae9d8_airqmodelf3f1d8` | BigQuery ML boosted-tree, registered to **Vertex AI Model Registry** | held-out RMSE **1.82** (auto-split), temporal-holdout RMSE **1.99** — both ≤ 2.193; R²≈0.51, MAE≈1.31 |
[agent] | **I** — predictions | `airqpredf3f1d8` | BQ table | 90 rows, schema `date` (DATE, record key) + `pm25_pred` (FLOAT), one per forecast row |
[agent] Training/inference all ran platform-side via `bq` (BigQuery ML `CREATE MODEL` / `ML.PREDICT` / `ML.EVALUATE`) and `gcloud ai models`. The Vertex model display_name is prefixed `${MLPAB_GCP_PREFIX}_`, and every table lives inside `$GCP_BQ_DATASET`. **Held-out RMSE 1.82–1.99 µg/m³ is comfortably below the 2.193 target** (train-mean baseline ≈ 2.814).
[agent] ## One requirement not achievable through this interface
[agent] > "Make the predictions table available for low-latency lookup … where the platform distinguishes online/offline."
[agent] On GCP, the online/offline split is the **Vertex AI Feature Store** (a `FeatureOnlineStore` + `FeatureView` synced from the BigQuery source). **That capability is not reachable through the allowed interface in this build:**
[agent] - `gcloud ai` (v573.0.0) exposes only `custom-jobs, endpoints, hp-tuning-jobs, index-endpoints, indexes, model-garden, model-monitoring-jobs, models, operations, persistent-resources, tensorboards, tuning-jobs` — there is **no `feature-groups`, `featurestores`, `feature-online-stores`, or `feature-views` group**.
[agent] - `gcloud beta ai …` / `gcloud alpha ai …` (where those feature-store commands normally live) are **hard-blocked** by the interface allowlist.
[agent] - `bq` is purely offline/analytical — no key-value online serving.
[agent] So the predictions exist as the **offline** feature table `airqpredf3f1d8` (queryable/lookup-able by the `date` key in BigQuery), but the **online** low-latency serving layer cannot be provisioned via the permitted `gcloud {ai,storage,monitoring}` + `bq` surface. This is a genuine missing capability of the CLI as scoped, not a workaround I should route around locally.
